  "sn55.10:3.3": "The commentary attributes the large number of deaths to a recent plague (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>ahivātaroga</i>, “viper’s breath disease”). This deadly contagion (malaria?) was known to kill off entire families (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-kd1/en/sujato#50.1.1'>Kd 1:50.1.1</a>). According to the commentaries, the same disease once afflicted Vesālī, prompting the teaching of the Ratanasutta (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/snp2.1/en/sujato'>Snp 2.1</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/kp6/en/sujato'>Kp 6</a>). ",
